User journey (attached Proof of Work, Section B)
1. AEAs keep recording daily prices and arrivals. The system ingests them nightly and alerts AEAs to missing days or implausible prices.
2. Each week the system harmonises the data, retrains, forecasts one to four weeks ahead, applies the skill gate and decision rules, and drafts advisories in Assamese and English.
3. An AMIU analyst approves, edits or holds each advisory in a review console.
4. Farmers receive an SMS, WhatsApp card or voice call; AEAs get a dashboard and a printable sheet for farmer meetings.
5. The farmer sells, holds or stores, and may report the price received. Forecasts are scored against actual prices on a public scorecard.
6. Before each sowing season, AEAs and planners receive crop-planning cards.

